847	+**Unreleased — earned guards and open voices** (cycle-129, [CHANGELOG](CHANGELOG.md)):
848	+
849	+- **Every guard carries its origin and its yield**: `grimoires/loa/guards.md` lists every hook, fence pattern, validator rule and gate with where it came from and whether it is active, dormant or telemetry; `.run/guard-yield.json` counts its real blocks and likely false positives over 30 days; `/loa` prints a Guards line. `guard-yield.sh --check` fails CI when a guard has no origin.
850	+- **Control arms**: the recall evals can run with a kernel block, the companion voice or the rule files switched off (`run-arms.sh`), against a record corpus of eight real sprints, so a rule's claim on review recall is measured before its text is cut. The kernel kept every pinned rationale this cycle (the arm run was still running at the gate) and shrank by the Agent Teams table; its byte cap fell to 9,445 B.
851	+- **Controls that run or go**: `implement_gate.mode` (`ask`, the default, logs a row; `telemetry`; `deny` refuses an unsanctioned App-Zone write while the run position is known), run position derived from files (`run-checkpoint.sh derive`), the circuit breaker as a script (`record-round`), per-task surgical-diff state; the input guardrails and danger-level enforcement default off in the example (82 events, zero catches), the Agent Teams rules live in their reference, and the pure-review skills carry `disallowed-tools`.
852	+- **The fence stops blocking prose**: a heredoc whose consumer only writes a file (`cat`, `tee`, `gh pr comment -F -`, `git commit -F -`, …) is scanned per segment, not as a command; interpreters, wrappers, substitutions, executable targets and anything unlisted still scan in full (`destructive_command_guard.heredoc_classifier`, corpus 99 benign / 184 dangerous rows). Two pre-existing holes closed on the way: a backtick substitution was inert to every rule, and `gh api` with a destructive method on refs, branch protection, tags, releases or the repository had no rule (`FR-GH-1`).
853	+- **One profile knob**: `loa.profile: lean | standard | full` sets the nine optional surfaces; no floor key is reachable through it; the example ships those keys as commented, profile-governed lines so a copied example follows the profile you choose, and `/loa` says when a guardrail control is off.
854	+- **Task kinds**: every sprint task says whether it is mechanical, judgment or operator work, and `tools/cycle-ratio.sh` prints the cycle's script / prose / model-call ratio.
855	+- **Open voices**: a local OpenAI-compatible server is a declared provider (`keyless: true`, `allow_insecure_endpoint: "127.0.0.1"`; one endpoint rule in cheval, the bash validator and `model-health-probe.sh --provider <name>`), the chat path sends `response_format` json_schema and strips thinking traces honestly, `advisory_voices` run beside the dissent's counted voices and can never change a verdict, and `hounfour.locality: local_voices` refuses every hosted hop by name across the dissent, Flatline, Bridgebuilder and the probe. Bridgebuilder reads providers only from trusted configuration, prints `completed/planned` voices and exits 3 on a degraded consensus.
856	+
