{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/hop-locality.py","line":116,"code_snippet":"group = entry.get(\"dispatch_group\") or block.get(\"dispatch_group\") or \"\"\nif group != \"local\":","reasoning_trace":"Traced the local_voices decision in hop-locality.py:116, config.ts:726-732 (isLocalVoice), modelinv.py:476 (hop_locality_of) and the loader's validate_providers (endpoint_policy.py:172): every classifier reads the dispatch_group label only; no code compares the provider endpoint host with the loopback/RFC1918/localhost rule check_insecure_optin encodes. Reproduced on head: provider acme at https://api.acme.example/v1 with model dispatch_group: local loads without refusal, hop-locality.py prints 'acme local dispatch_group=local', hop_telemetry returns hop_locality local with destination.host api.acme.example.","finding":"Under hounfour.locality: local_voices a hosted https provider labelled dispatch_group: local is planned, dispatched and audited as local; the endpoint host is never checked.","critique":"The posture's whole promise is that model calls stay local; a label is not a verified property. The audit row asserts hop_locality: local for a public host (destination is recorded truthfully, which is the only mitigation).","remediation":"Define the local-hop rule once (HTTP provider whose endpoint host passes check_insecure_optin acceptance) and apply it in validate_providers (refuse at load), hop-locality.py, isLocalVoice (carry endpoint in ProviderDecl) and hop_locality_of; add the mislabelled case to test_config_examples_load.py, adversarial-review-locality.bats and trusted-config.test.ts.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-807","CWE-1288","SDD D-8.0","SDD D-8.1"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/resources/config.ts","line":685,"code_snippet":"const keylessOnlyInHead = decl.keyless && t?.keyless !== true;\nconst insecureOnlyInHead = decl.insecure && t?.insecure !== true;","reasoning_trace":"loadTrustedConfig computes headOnlyRefused from two booleans (keyless, insecure present); the endpoint, opt-in host and auth template are never compared. config.trusted (main.ts:464) is read only by validateApiKeys and the pipeline keyless check; every voice is dispatched via ChevalDelegateAdapter, which resolves cheval.py from process.cwd() (cheval-delegate.ts:117, unchanged) and cheval loads the working tree's .loa.config.yaml. Reproduced: head cheval loader admits openai.endpoint https://evil.example.invalid/v1 with auth {env:OPENAI_API_KEY} (validate_declared_endpoint skips the allowlist). SKILL.md:118 newly claims the keys follow the trusted source even on a PR-head checkout.","finding":"Bridgebuilder's trusted configuration gates admission only; on a PR-head checkout a head that re-points a trusted provider's endpoint or re-declares a built-in provider is admitted and dispatched by cheval with the runner credential, contradicting SKILL.md:118.","critique":"The exposure predates the change (base cheval had no endpoint validation at all); the change claims to close it and does not. The gate compares booleans, not the endpoint and credential it is meant to protect.","remediation":"On a pull request compute head-vs-trusted drift over hounfour.providers (endpoint, auth, opt-in host, keyless, dispatch_group), aliases, locality and secret_env_allowlist and refuse with a distinct exit code; or write the trusted config to a temp path and pass it to cheval. Correct SKILL.md:118 to the invocation model the protection assumes.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-345","OWASP-A08:2021","SDD D-7.5","DEC-0170"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":1813,"code_snippet":"_chain, _models_not_planned = _plan_around_agy(_chain, hounfour)","reasoning_trace":"cheval plans around the agy opt-in but has no equivalent for hounfour.locality; it records locality_mode via hop_telemetry only. locality_mode_of (modelinv.py:466-471) returns None for an unknown value and the row omits the field; the loader never validates the key. Only adversarial-review.sh, flatline-orchestrator.sh, Bridgebuilder and (claimed) the probe gate the posture.","finding":"cheval never enforces local_voices itself and never validates the hounfour.locality value; any other caller dispatches hosted hops under the posture, and a local alias's catalog fallback_chain is walked inside one call.","critique":"The guarantee holds only for the four patched planners.","remediation":"Validate hounfour.locality in load_config; under local_voices refuse a hop whose hop_locality is not local (failure_class locality_refused), including fallback-chain hops.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-693"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"documentation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/loa/reference/scripts-reference.md","line":73,"code_snippet":"| `model-health-probe.sh [--provider <name>]` | ... refuses a hosted probe under `local_voices`. |","reasoning_trace":"scripts-reference.md:73 and multi-model-reference.md:102 (and the example comment at :818) say the health probe is covered by the posture. grep -i 'locality|local_voices' over head/.claude/scripts/model-health-probe.sh returns nothing; _probe_configured (:1434) and the built-in probes read no locality key.","finding":"Documentation claims the health probe refuses hosted probes under local_voices; the probe has no locality code.","critique":"A documented security control that does not exist.","remediation":"Implement the gate in model-health-probe.sh (same yq tag check as the planners; refuse built-in and non-local configured providers) with a bats case, or remove the claim from both references and the example.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1059"]}
{"id":"DEV-001","category":"devops","criterion":"reliability","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/model-health-probe.sh","line":1475,"code_snippet":"if ! endpoint_validator__check \"${_vflags[@]}\" \"$url\" >/dev/null 2>\"$verr\"; then","reasoning_trace":"_probe_configured validates <endpoint>/models with --allowlist (validate(), _declared_endpoint=False) so step 8's host allowlist applies; the cheval loader uses validate_declared_endpoint which skips it. A configured https host not in loa-providers.json (the PR's Azure example) loads in cheval but is refused by the probe as ENDPOINT-NOT-ALLOWED (review reproduced it; the code path is unambiguous).","finding":"The probe applies the hosted host allowlist to configured providers; the PR's own Azure example is refused.","critique":"Two different rules for the same declared endpoint.","remediation":"Add a declared-endpoint mode to the validator CLI mapped to validate_declared_endpoint, or document that only allowlisted or opted-in hosts are probeable.","confidence":"high","references":["SDD D-7.5"]}
{"id":"DEV-002","category":"devops","criterion":"configuration","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/adversarial-review.sh","line":4335,"code_snippet":"if [[ $estimated_cost_cents -gt $budget ]]; then","reasoning_trace":"_adv_budget_estimate (:4333) sums primary + companion first hop + each advisory voice at catalog prices. Head catalog: gpt-5.3-codex 1.75/14, gpt-5.5-pro 30/180, claude-headless 10/50 USD per Mtok. 100 KB diff = 33,833 tokens: 7c at gpt-5.3-codex, 137c at gpt-5.5-pro (old fixed formula 39c); plus claude-headless ~43c exceeds the unchanged example default 150. .loa.config.yaml.example:1624 and :1690 still say 'ONE dissent call'.","finding":"The budget gate was recalibrated to every planned voice at catalog prices while the example default budget_cents: 150 and its 'ONE dissent call' comment were not.","critique":"Gates refused on moderate diffs for operators on the example default with a premium primary; the comment misdescribes the gate.","remediation":"Update both comments; raise or document the default; add a Migration note.","confidence":"high","references":["SDD D-7.4","SDD D-7.6"]}
{"id":"DEV-003","category":"devops","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/skills/scheduled-cycle-template/contracts/session-cap-bb/dispatcher.sh","line":78,"code_snippet":"if [[ \"$rc\" -eq 3 ]]; then\n    degraded=true","reasoning_trace":"Any exit 3 from $BB_ENTRY is recorded degraded: true and the dispatcher exits 0 (:89) without checking that $BB_OUT holds a run JSON with a verdicts array. LOA_SESSION_CAP_BB_ENTRY (:57) may name a pre-cycle-129 entry.sh whose missing-zod preflight exits 3.","finding":"dispatcher.sh accepts any exit 3 as a completed-degraded review without a run JSON.","critique":"A review that never ran can be recorded as completed.","remediation":"Accept 3 as completion only when jq -e '.verdicts | type == \"array\"' \"$BB_OUT\" succeeds; otherwise keep it a failure.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-754"]}
